In the evening I walked back to the station.
I got onto the next S-Bahn.
It had already gotten dark outside.
Nobody talked in the carriage.
The other day-trippers fell asleep over their backpacks.
I leaned my head against the window.
I looked out at the dark pine forests again.
The train drove quickly through the night.
Then I finally arrived in Berlin.
I got out of the train.
I walked slowly to my flat.
I came home really late.
I am totally tired now, Sofia.
But I am also completely happy.
I really liked spring in Potsdam.
I will call you tomorrow, good night!
